{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9833","id":4763426868,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLj5faM8AAAABG-wgNA","html_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9833","diff_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9833.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9833.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9833","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9833/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9833/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9833/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/statuses/b65be4c9550c5097f0a3add08933531a1c24d534","number":9833,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[grug] Compute the MoE routing-weight gradient on the expert side","user":{"login":"mcwitt","id":319411,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTQxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt","html_url":"https://github.com/mcwitt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The hero takes its MoE routing-weight gradient from the expert MLP's own backward, so the backward needs neither the expert outputs nor their return transport, and the hero saves the routed output instead of recomputing the expert down projection, the return all-to-all and the combine. The step shortens by 3.14% (13.542 to 13.130 s). Peak HBM rises by ~20 GiB to ~125 GiB of the 143.75 GiB pool.\n\n`moe_mlp` and `MoEExpertMlp` gain `routing_weight_gradient`. The default, `EXACT`, keeps the expert outputs and differentiates the combine, as before. `EXPERT_SIDE` is the new path, which the hero selects; other implementations reject it. Where w * dout rounds to zero in the cotangent dtype (a zero weight, or in float16 a normal weight times a small cotangent), its gradient is zero or inexact. The hero's routing weights are positive renormalized sigmoids and its cotangents bf16, which has fp32's exponent range. Forward, dx, dW13 and dW2 are bitwise unchanged; the routing-weight gradient differs at bf16 rounding (median ~1 ulp) at nonzero weights.\n\nThe gradient with respect to the combine weight w[t,k] is dS[t,k] = <dout[t], y[t,k]>, the only backward consumer of the expert down projection's output y. Since dy = w * dout and dh = dy W2^T, the same value is rowsum(dh * h) / w, built from tensors the expert MLP backward already holds. One custom VJP from dispatch to combine returns s = <h, dh> per expert row, sends it back with one [C, 1] f32 all-to-all per chunk, and forms dS = s / w in f32; dropped and padded slots get 0 by selection. The portable `ragged_dot` expert MLP, used without QuACK, still keeps its outputs for the row dot. The backward's transports reuse the forward transfers' offsets, swapped, and on GPU its weighted output cotangents come from #9832's scatter kernel.\n\nThe saved routed output needs a larger remat budget, so the carry offload defaults to a 0.78 memory fraction and an XLA memory-limit slop factor of 105 (114 GiB, against 87.7 GiB at 0.75 and 85, below the backward's ~105 GiB). With the backward's transports no longer ordered after the recompute's, several collectives in flight gave run-to-run different gradients or hung on GB200, so every ragged run forces a collective overlap limit of 1.\n\nStep times are single runs on one 64-GPU hero rack (restore step-180000, seed 0, 100 steps) from #9708's measurements.\n\nSplit from #9708. Part of #9636.\n","labels":[{"id":10166074947,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACXfH-Qw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agent-generated","name":"agent-generated","description":"Created by automation/agent","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11981276996,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACyiPHRA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agentic-lint","name":"agentic-lint","description":"Local agentic lint review completed","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-06T19:07:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T20:08:22Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"365a91478f030eed287edaac0eb84c62aba8c3ee","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dlwh","id":9633,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9633?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh","html_url":"https://github.com/dlwh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/received_events","type":